' What "debug in the cluster" is, between pressing it and stopping somewhere.
'
' Needs Graphviz, like cluster.puml. It describes what the native examples in
' this repository actually do — odin-hello, zig-hello, rust-hello and the two
' C ones all take this path.

@startuml
title Debug in the cluster, from the press to the breakpoint

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Building : press debug

Building --> Pushing : a binary for the pod's architecture
Building --> [*] : it did not compile

Pushing --> Waiting : copied in, started under the debug server

Waiting : the process is up and held
Waiting : before its first instruction

Waiting --> Attached : the debugger connects
Attached --> Stopped : a breakpoint, or a signal
Stopped --> Attached : continue
Stopped --> [*] : stop
Attached --> [*] : detach — the pod goes with it

note right of Waiting
  Held, not racing: a program that would be
  over before the debugger arrived is the
  reason for the wait.
end note

@enduml
